## TL013 dashboard-authenticated metadata resync continuation (2026-10-31)

- First sync POST returned HTTP 403 before its handler. Source branch `src/server/authz/policies/management.ts:331-336` identifies cause: supplied DB API-key value was not valid management bearer (`api_keys.key` did not validate against management `key_hash`). Exact source response for this invalid-Bearer branch: `{"error":{"code":"AUTH_001","message":"Invalid management token","correlation_id":"<request-id>"}}`. Dynamic correlation ID and original body were not retained. No evidence points to Origin, CSRF, session, Host, or deliberate `/api/v1` deny middleware. Invalid request did not run importer.
- Used existing dashboard password login and native session cookie, same-origin `Origin`, and `x-omniroute-csrf` token from `/api/auth/csrf`. Login, CSRF fetch, and `/api/settings/models-dev?action=status` returned 200. Exactly one native POST with `{"action":"sync","dryRun":false,"syncCapabilities":false}` then returned HTTP 200, `success=true`, 9,829 models, 238 providers, 0 capability writes. No arbitrary retry, new credential, JWT construction, scope grant, auth/middleware/config change. Before status had `lastSync=null`, `periodicEnabled=false`; route awaits sync result and returns it. Status omits an `inProgress` field, so no separate concurrent-work claim is made. `periodicEnabled=false` remained after sync.
- Protected SQLite online backup before successful mutation, integrity `ok`, mode 0600, 95,899,648 bytes, SHA-256 `fcfd8950cb3ce9d624ed16bf095f4522d3e4c87e06a2c0f8771892aeb6834b7d`: `/var/oled/omniroute-deploy-diagnostics/e013-41235613024-dashboard-auth-pre-sync.sqlite`. Before capture `e013-41235613024-dashboard-auth-before.json` (9,162 bytes, SHA-256 `5764fb5948d293f86680e2c41dee46c0d6f5ecde387e465238381a7ea18d8581`); after capture `e013-41235613024-dashboard-auth-after.json` (9,731 bytes, SHA-256 `a33c0c6ccd8b7fe4237bff0553821d7e402bb9210a4c3c8e4069a922ab0cf24c`). Captures and backup remain mode 0600.
